.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt MEMBARRIER 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm membarrier
.Nd a memory barrier on the processors that run a process's threads
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In linux/membarrier.h
.In sys/syscall.h
.In unistd.h
.Ft int
.Fn syscall SYS_membarrier "int cmd" "unsigned int flags" "int cpu_id"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn membarrier
makes each processor that runs a thread of the caller's process, or of
any process, pass a full memory barrier before it returns, so that a
program can leave the barrier out of its fast path and pay for it on the
slow one.
User-space RCU, garbage collectors and the .NET runtime issue it.
It answers as Linux 6.12's call does on x86, which has the sync-core
commands, with the rseq commands of a kernel that has
.Xr rseq 2 .
.Fa cmd
is one of:
.Bl -tag -width MEMBARRIER_CMD_PRIVATE_EXPEDITED_SYNC_CORE
.It Dv MEMBARRIER_CMD_QUERY
Return the mask of the commands, 0x3FF: every one below.
.It Dv MEMBARRIER_CMD_GLOBAL
Wait until every processor that runs a thread, of any process, has passed
a barrier.
.It Dv MEMBARRIER_CMD_GLOBAL_EXPEDITED
The same, for the processors that run a thread of a process registered
with
.Dv MEMBARRIER_CMD_REGISTER_GLOBAL_EXPEDITED ;
the caller needs no registration.
.It Dv MEMBARRIER_CMD_REGISTER_GLOBAL_EXPEDITED
Register the caller's process as a target of the command above.
.It Dv MEMBARRIER_CMD_PRIVATE_EXPEDITED
Wait until every processor that runs a thread of the caller's process has
passed a barrier.
.It Dv MEMBARRIER_CMD_REGISTER_PRIVATE_EXPEDITED
Register for the command above, which fails with
.Er EPERM
before.
.It Dv MEMBARRIER_CMD_PRIVATE_EXPEDITED_SYNC_CORE
The same, with a serializing instruction on each of those processors and
the caller's, so code one thread wrote runs as written on the others.
A thread of the process switched to later is serialized too.
.It Dv MEMBARRIER_CMD_REGISTER_PRIVATE_EXPEDITED_SYNC_CORE
Register for the command above.
.It Dv MEMBARRIER_CMD_PRIVATE_EXPEDITED_RSEQ
The same as the private barrier, and each thread it reaches has the rseq
critical section it is in aborted before it runs on.
With
.Dv MEMBARRIER_CMD_FLAG_CPU
in
.Fa flags
it reaches processor
.Fa cpu_id
alone, the caller's included, and nothing when that processor is not
started or runs no thread of the process.
.It Dv MEMBARRIER_CMD_REGISTER_PRIVATE_EXPEDITED_RSEQ
Register for the command above.
.It Dv MEMBARRIER_CMD_GET_REGISTRATIONS
Return the registration commands the process has made, as a mask.
The sync-core and rseq registrations count as
.Dv MEMBARRIER_CMD_REGISTER_PRIVATE_EXPEDITED
too, as on Linux, though they do not allow the plain private barrier.
.El
.Pp
The registrations belong to the address space: the threads of a process
share them, a
.Xr fork 2
child takes its parent's, and an
.Xr execve 2
clears them.
A private barrier of a process with one thread, or on a machine with one
processor started, returns at once, but for the sync-core one.
.Pp
The caller's processor holds the big kernel lock through the call, so no
processor switches threads meanwhile; each other processor the command
names is sent an interprocessor interrupt and answers it with a locked
exchange, a full barrier, after an
.Ic iret
to the next instruction for the sync-core command.
A processor in the kernel or idle runs no thread of a process and passes a
barrier when it next takes the lock.
.Ss System call interface
The call is number 375 on i386 and 324 on x86-64, and 375 for an i386
program on the x86-64 kernel
.Pq Xr ia32 7 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv MEMBARRIER_CMD_QUERY
and
.Dv MEMBARRIER_CMD_GET_REGISTRATIONS
return their masks and the other commands 0.
The raw call returns a negative error number on failure;
.Fn syscall
instead returns -1 and sets
.Va errno .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Pa tests/membarrierprobe.c
queries the commands, checks that each private barrier fails before its
registration and passes after it, reads the registrations back, runs the
barriers with a second thread spinning on another processor, and checks
the refusals of an unknown command and of flags.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width "[EINVAL]"
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Fa cmd
is not a command,
.Fa flags
is not 0, or, for
.Dv MEMBARRIER_CMD_PRIVATE_EXPEDITED_RSEQ ,
neither 0 nor
.Dv MEMBARRIER_CMD_FLAG_CPU .
.It Bq Er EPERM
A private command came before the process registered for it.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr futex 2 ,
.Xr rseq 2
